  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's estimation accuracy is dependent on local cycling rates, performing better in cities that already have a higher cycling modal share.",
      "what": "The researchers developed a framework to estimate relative urban cycling intensity by weighting openly accessible Strava Global Heatmap data with population and point of interest (POI) counts. They validated this approach against official cycle count data from 29 cities across Europe and North America, finding strong correlations (Spearman's rho > 0.7 for all, and > 0.8 for most cities), with POI-weighting performing best.",
      "why": "It provides a low-effort, globally consistent method to estimate spatial cycling volumes in cities where official physical counter infrastructure is sparse or non-existent."
    }
